{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The words of Amos…who was among the shepherds of Tekoa</b>: This prophet was in the days of Hoshea, and most of his prophecy was concerning Jeroboam son of Joash. Most of the commentators said that the earthquake was when Uzziah entered to burn incense, but there is no proof from Scripture, only from tradition. For Scripture says that the earthquake was in the days of Uzziah, and it was a great thing, and by this reckoning it is \"and that within sixty-five years\" — for if this prophecy was at the beginning of the reign of Ahaz, then after twenty-two years Ephraim will be shattered by the people of Assyria, for so it is written. And the reason for mentioning the earthquake is that he prophesied before it came to pass, that an earthquake would come and strike the winter house upon the summer house." "<b>and among the herdsmen</b> (נוקדים): shepherds, as in: \"and Mesha king of Moab was a herdman\" (נוקד)."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The citation 'and that within sixty-five years' likely alludes to Isaiah 7:8; the logic connecting it to Amos's dating is compressed and the clause 'כי אם היתה זאת הנבואה' may refer to Amos's prophecy being read retroactively from Isaiah's era."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:44.552889492Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}